From de3f1e3377432c8e7b951194482d54177c9a2ff5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Andrey Stoyan <andrey.stoyan.csam@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 15 Aug 2026 14:11:09 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 16/43] test(chexc): performs syntax fixes; drop unimplemented
 conversions/adapt cases

The performs cases now pass against the implementation:
- 'handle' takes a single pattern and 'resume with v' -- there is no named
  Resumption parameter, which the first draft assumed;
- stdx-dependent cases use the suite's %enableEH, which supplies the
  stdx.effect import path along with --experimental --enable-eh.

Removes the conversions/ and adapt/ groups. They were committed red-first for
features that are not implemented, so every suite run reported 5 failures that
had to be explained away as expected -- which is how a real regression gets
overlooked. They are restored on their own branches together with the
implementations they describe (chexc-conversions, chexc-adapt).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
